<title>CHILE: Codelco/Australia firm in Peru copper deal talks.</title>
<headline>Codelco/Australia firm in Peru copper deal talks.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minera Los Andes, a joint venture between Chile's state copper company Codelco and Australian fund manager AMP, is in talks to invest in a copper project in Peru, said a top Los Andes official.</p>
<p>&quot;We are in negotiations to buy a large copper deposit in Peru,&quot; Los Andes general manager Nicolas Saric told Reuters.</p>
<p>Saric said Los Andes was interested in developing projects with output of at least 60,000 tonnes a year which could have a major effect on the firm's cash flow.</p>
</text>
